oad, Atlanta, Georgia. Its common stock trades on the New York Stock Exchange under the ticker symbol GPN. Zavia’s registry data additionally records a Washington Secretary of State filing for Global Payments Inc. (UBI 602186332, effective 2 November 2010), listed as Active; this reflects the company’s registration to transact business in Washington rather than its state of incorporation.\n\nGlobal Payments Inc. operates as a commerce enablement company, providing payment processing, point-of-sale technology and business management software to merchants and software partners. Its offerings combine card and digital payment acceptance with integrated software for scheduling, inventory, payroll and other business functions, delivered directly and through independent software vendors and financial institution partnerships across sectors including retail, restaurants, professional services, healthcare and education.\n\nGlobal Payments Inc. reports operations spanning North America, Europe, the Asia-Pacific region and Latin America, with approximately 26,000 employees across 37 countries as of 31 December 2025, according to its Form 10-K for the year ended 31 December 2025. For fiscal year 2025, the company reported consolidated GAAP revenue of approximately $10.1 billion, an increase of 4.7% from the prior year, and adjusted net revenue of approximately $9.32 billion; these are consolidated figures for the group rather than figures for any single legal entity within it.\n\nOn 17 April 2025, Global Payments Inc. announced agreements to acquire Worldpay from FIS Inc. and GTCR, in a transaction valued at approximately $24.25 billion, while simultaneously agreeing to divest its Issuer Solutions business – the card-issuer processing operations historically associated with the TSYS brand – to FIS for approximately $13.5 billion. Both transactions completed on 9 January 2026, after which the company described itself as a pure-play merchant and commerce solutions provider, with FIS assuming the Issuer Solutions business and Global Payments Inc. taking full ownership of Worldpay.\n\nData Provenance\n\nThis record is sourced directly from official government registries, including Washington Secretary of State.\n\n[View data sources →](https://zavia.ai/data-coverage/)\n\nWe don’t stop at registry data.\n\nEvery company record is enriched with additional intelligence:\n\n* Company fundamentals\n* Corporate linkage & group structures\n* Digitized company financials\n* Firmographics — websites, social profiles, revenue and employee estimates\n\n[View full data dictionary →](https://zavia.ai/data-dictionary-2/)\n\n## Shareholders\n\n4\n\n#### Shareholders of Global Payments Inc.\n\nZavia’s shareholder register lists four disclosed holdings in Global Payments Inc. as of 2 August 2026: Vanguard Group Inc (16.09%), Columbia Fd.s Series TRT II-Columbia Seligman Technology and Informati fund (3.02%), iShares Trust-iShares Core S&P 500 ETF (2.14%), and Fidelity Concord Street Trust-Fidelity 500 Index Fund (2.08%). Vanguard Group Inc is the largest disclosed holder. Every shareholder on record is an institutional asset manager or index-tracking fund rather than an individual, and all interests are recorded as direct ordinary-share holdings as of the stated date. As a New York Stock Exchange-listed company, Global Payments Inc. is not required to maintain a public register of its complete shareholder base; the holdings shown here represent a subset of its wider institutional ownership, broadly consistent with the type of holder that discloses stakes to the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission under Schedule 13D/13G, and should not be read as a complete shareholder list.\n\n#### Data availability\n\nShareholder information for Global Payments Inc. is available only for major institutional holders rather than its full shareholder base, consistent with standard U.S. disclosure practice for New York Stock Exchange-listed companies; retail holdings and other stakes below applicable reporting thresholds are not captured in this data.\n\n#### Sources\n\n* Zavia.ai shareholder register data for Global Payments Inc., data date 2 August 2026, retrieved 9 September 2026.\n* U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, EDGAR filing index for Global Payments Inc. (CIK 0001123360), Schedule 13D/13G filings, https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0001123360&type=SC+13, retrieved 9 September 2026.\n\n| Shareholder | Type | Holding | Source Document |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Vanguard Group Inc | Entity | 16.1% | Washington Secretary of State |\n| Columbia Fd.s Series TRT II-Columbia Seligman Technology and Informati | Entity | 3% | Washington Secretary of State |\n| iShares Trust-iShares Core S&P 500 ETF | Entity | 2.1% | Washington Secretary of State |\n| Fidelity Concord Street Trust-Fidelity 500 Index Fund | Entity | 2.1% | Washington Secretary of State |\n\nView all shareholders & beneficial ownership\n\nFull cap table, ownership percentages, and ultimate beneficial owners resolved down to the natural person.\n\n[View all shareholders →](https://zavia.ai/price/)\n\n## Officers\n\n11\n\n#### Directors and officers of Global Payments Inc.\n\nZavia’s registry data includes a Washington Secretary of State filing for Global Payments Inc. listing 41 officer records across nine pages under the role \"Governor,\" including William I. Jacobs, John M. Partridge, Mitchell L. Hollin, Michael W. Trapp and Jeffrey S. Sloan, all shown with work status \"Active\" and no appointment or resignation dates. Checked against Global Payments Inc.’s own public disclosures, this filing is outdated: Jeffrey S. Sloan stepped down as Chief Executive Officer and resigned from the Board of Directors effective 1 June 2023, succeeded as CEO by Cameron M. Bready. According to the company’s proxy statement filed 13 March 2026, its Board of Directors is chaired by Troy Woods and currently comprises thirteen directors. The Washington 